{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794680923,"nonce":"JZDCsqymKfLuHArh8/RABDdY3VU=","title":"Text in a card that is scaled and faded is drawn from a base-size bitmap and magnified","message":"A labelled card scaled 1x to 2x by a CSS keyframe animation and held there. Without a fade the label is as sharp as the same label laid out at 2x (sharpness ratio 1.00 on the Vector, Table and Rows paths of the animation_paths harness). With a fade in the same keyframes it is 0.59 as sharp on all three.\n\nText in an opacity group goes through prepare_captured_text, which lays it out at the base size and leaves the card's affine to magnify it; only the node table's branch rasterized at the shown size. The ungrouped text paths already did (23b08b1b, 1e213504).\n\nFixed by rasterizing grouped text outside the table at its affine's scale: 1.04 settled, and in flight as sharp as unfaded text. The size is rounded up to a quarter only while an animation of the scale plays, since the group tests compare an animated frame of an opacity-only animation with a static reference and need the same raster.\n\nIn flight all text is softer than at rest, see 879382f.","files":null}]}